  "decision": null,
  "decisions": [],
  "log": "This is the exact content gap behind Role-level/Organizational-level. Per Tim (Sept 15, 2026): the existing AI Transition Pathways self-assessment/TMI tool is explicitly NOT to be used to fill this — that's GiGi's separate lane. So this remains fully unserved. The Shock Wave Effect's own “Open Questions” (Manager and Team measurement) names an overlapping but distinct gap — no instrument built for either.\n\nSept 29, 2026: acceptance extended with GiGi's condition from her GR-001 approval — the instrument's results must show their drivers and evidence, since the readiness verdict beside each ceiling draws on them.\n\nSept 29, 2026: GiGi sent Human Operating Readiness Instrument v0.1, her working draft for this requirement: ten dimensions, each giving a Green / Yellow / Red / Gray finding with its evidence rather than a single score; six potential hard gates to pressure-test; a first pressure test on HRBP Manager / employee grievances (verdict: Insufficient Evidence); a proposed assessment record; and seven questions for Tim. Added to the WIP hub under External & Partner Review Notes (gigi_gr012_human_operating_readiness.html, with her original PDF).\n\nLater Sept 29, 2026: GiGi sent her own review of v0.1 (gigi_gr012_review_thoughts.html): keep the instrument, refine rather than rethink. Her refinements before v0.1 is treated as a proposed spec: group the ten dimensions into role-level and organizational-level conditions, with Trust / Evidence Quality at the boundary (it consumes the technical/process lane's evidence rather than re-running it); mark findings Gray, not Yellow, where there is no organization-specific evidence, recording the modeled concern separately; rename Manager Readiness to Manager / Oversight Readiness so it works for executive roles; and let the first pilots decide which dimensions are hard gates. Her sequence: revise, rerun the HRBP grievance pilot manually with evidence requirements per dimension, then Recruiter and CHRO, then GR-013. Both documents came with her email 'Decisions & GR-012 Review', which adds that for executive roles the oversight relationship may be a governance body rather than a traditional manager.\n\nLater Sept 29, 2026 (Tim): the grievance pilot pack prepared for the working session (grievance_pilot_pack.html). Tim decided 7.4.4 stays one activity in the reference model for now: the pilot worksheet splits the work into parts (intake, precedent research, case preparation, documentation, determination, escalation), and the parts past the Judgment ceiling are flagged as findings about a transition the reference model does not allow at Critical Consequence of Error. Whether processes with no APQC activities (18 in PCF 7.0) should get framework activities of their own is decided once, as a pattern, after the pilots. The pack also holds the technical-evidence line Trust / Evidence Quality consumes, a worksheet built on GiGi's assessment record with every finding starting Gray, and Tim's draft answers to her seven questions. Proposed, awaiting GiGi's agreement: acceptance wording changes from 'scores all 10 readiness dimensions' to 'produces a finding, with its evidence, for each of the ten dimensions'.",
  "legacy_status": "Open"
