  "log": "Sept 25, 2026 scan. Sandbox 7.0 (docs/sandbox/pcf7.html): no view displays Future State, but every one of the 118 WR_DATA entries carries a future value, the WR data mapping copies it (future: d.future || null), the L3 coverage helper accepts 'future' as a field, and the classification comments above WR_DATA describe “Future = Ceiling”. In 117 of 118 activities future equals ceiling, so removing it loses nothing. The exception is 7.2.1.3 (future Oversight, ceiling Agent-delegation). It is the explicit-governance-policy freeze example in GR-041, so Tim and GiGi decide whether its ceiling becomes Oversight before the field goes; either way the change is logged in changelog-data.js. CI: scripts/check-changelog-audit.mjs checks WR_DATA rel/future/ceiling and must drop future in the same change. WIP documents that use the term: index.html, talking_through_your_questions.html, five_worked_examples.html, the three pattern-transition stage-first pages (recruiter, HRBP Manager, CHRO), gigi_website_framework_review.html and gigi_reflections_updated.html. GiGi's review documents are her record and keep their original wording; the fix there is a note, not a rewrite. Also covers the WR Progression Methodology source (section 3) and the “Understanding Working-Relationship Progression” page. Register: GR-028 and GR-041 cite “section 3, Current State, Future State, Progression Ceiling” and GR-035 says “future-state check”; update those. GR-019 and GR-043 use “future” in its ordinary sense and need no change. Production is out of scope until the full production rebuild. Sept 25, 2026 — cleanup pass done in Sandbox 7.0 and WIP: the future field removed from all 118 WR_DATA entries and the sandbox code that copied it, with every Current State and Progression Ceiling value unchanged; logged as CL-003 in changelog-data.js; the CI audit now tracks rel and ceiling only; the Production Changelog's “WR Future” label replaced with “WR Model Change”; the term removed from the WIP hub, Five Worked Examples, and the three pattern-transition stage-first pages (M5 subtitle now “End state”); GR-028, GR-035 and GR-041 reworded. 7.2.1.3 settled by Tim the same day: its ceiling moved down to Oversight because of its High Consequence of Error (CL-004). GiGi's reviews and Talking Through Your Questions use “future state” in the general org-design sense, in GiGi's own words, and are left as written. Still open: the section 3 heading in Working_Relationship_Progression_Methodology.docx; and the production pages (Understanding Working-Relationship Progression, the WR Progression Table), which wait for the production rebuild.\n\nSept 29, 2026 (Tim): the full methodology (HTML page, its PDF, the WIP copy of the PDF, and the Word file) no longer mentions Future State; its section 3 now reads “Current State and Progression Ceiling”.",
